1
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:17,150
Prince Gadiel has arrived.

2
00:00:27,970 --> 00:00:31,780
Oh? You're looking better than I expected.

3
00:00:32,710 --> 00:00:37,000
As Rovel and the others aren't with you,
 I presume they saw right through me.

4
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:38,820
What a shame.

5
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:41,640
You have my praise
 for returning with the medicine.

6
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:45,740
However, you do understand this was
 a gesture of Ellen's kindness, don't you?

7
00:00:45,740 --> 00:00:46,520
Yes.

8
00:00:48,030 --> 00:00:48,980
Father...

9
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:51,570
Father, did you use me as one of your pawns?!

10
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:53,440
What makes you think so?

11
00:00:54,190 --> 00:00:57,450
You ordered your subordinates to kidnap
a daughter of the Vankreift family,

12
00:00:57,450 --> 00:01:00,800
then sent me to procure 
medicine from their domain!

13
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:03,910
All to ensure I'd cross paths with them!

14
00:01:10,710 --> 00:01:12,990
I have a message from Ellen.

15
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:17,800
"You will regret ever touching
 my family," she said.

16
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:20,640
I see.

17
00:01:21,170 --> 00:01:25,820
She also said to never again 
make contact with the Vankreifts—

18
00:01:25,820 --> 00:01:27,600
That this is their final warning.

19
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:32,070
It seems I've angered Ellen.

20
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:36,310
Guard!

21
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:41,410
Inform the gatekeepers that entry
 to the royal capital is now restricted!

22
00:01:42,510 --> 00:01:45,020
Gather all the healers in the country!

23
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:46,270
At once!

24
00:01:46,270 --> 00:01:47,960
The queen and my sons will evacuate!

25
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:50,180
I cannot have them stay here!

26
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:50,890
Yes, sire!

27
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:57,150
I have made an enemy of the Vankreifts.

28
00:01:58,020 --> 00:02:01,300
The royal family will now face retribution.

29
00:02:02,690 --> 00:02:05,270
I misread Ellen.

30
00:02:05,270 --> 00:02:08,190
I assumed she was softhearted 
and underestimated her.

31
00:02:12,350 --> 00:02:14,050
Is this all the medicine?

32
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:14,910
Yes.

33
00:02:15,410 --> 00:02:17,410
I-If I may...

34
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:21,570
Th-This is far from enough
 to treat everyone in the country.

35
00:02:26,610 --> 00:02:30,390
King Ravisel has taken us too lightly.

36
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:36,590
After all he's done, do not think 
for a moment you will have our aid.

37
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,740
We've been given little medicine.

38
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:47,770
The royal capital will soon be flooded 
with patients and fall into chaos.

39
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:50,730
We have no choice but to restrict entry.

40
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:54,230
However, this could breed 
resentment and lead to riots.

41
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:59,990
Well, this will serve as a test for you.

42
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:03,010
Your Majesty.

43
00:03:05,630 --> 00:03:07,290
I shall stay here with you.

44
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:14,190
Very well. You've truly grown strong.

45
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:19,030
BETWEEN HUMANS AND SPIRITS

46
00:03:26,710 --> 00:03:32,290
Even if you wish to stay in this country, 
we cannot guarantee your lives.

47
00:03:32,290 --> 00:03:34,610
The royal family already 
has their eye on you.

48
00:03:35,050 --> 00:03:38,670
Of course, we will not 
allow you safe harbor here.

49
00:03:39,190 --> 00:03:41,860
Especially after all you've done to Rafilia.

50
00:03:41,860 --> 00:03:44,270
Hmph! So what?

51
00:03:44,270 --> 00:03:46,330
If you do as I'm about to say,

52
00:03:47,940 --> 00:03:49,780
we'll let you live.

53
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:53,620
Let's hear it.

54
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:58,790
Spread word that the royal family has 
seized all of what little medicine remained

55
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:02,060
from the treatment center 
in the Vankreift domain.

56
00:04:03,090 --> 00:04:06,550
Spread that rumor, and we'll assist you
 in fleeing the country.

57
00:04:10,070 --> 00:04:11,310
Fine.

58
00:04:12,730 --> 00:04:14,580
Much obliged.

59
00:04:15,230 --> 00:04:17,470
Please see them off the property.

60
00:04:17,470 --> 00:04:18,200
Yes, milady.

61
00:04:21,210 --> 00:04:24,880
Oh, and please don't get any funny ideas.

62
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:28,390
The spirit queen is always 
watching over you, after all.

63
00:04:29,790 --> 00:04:30,770
Move it.

64
00:04:35,110 --> 00:04:38,990
If the king handles this poorly, 
the royal family is sure to perish.

65
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:43,060
Well, I'm sure with Mr. Blackheart, 
they'll be just fine.

66
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:43,950
Ellen...

67
00:04:45,050 --> 00:04:48,180
We mustn't forgive them. It will only
make the royal family arrogant.

68
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:50,160
Yes, but this is...

69
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:50,640
Uncle.

70
00:04:51,510 --> 00:04:53,600
Please restrict entry into our domain.

71
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:58,560
Tell any new patients that our medicine 
was taken by the royal family.

72
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,790
Also, please spread word that Father and I

73
00:05:02,790 --> 00:05:06,010
have gone to gather medicinal ingredients.

74
00:05:06,010 --> 00:05:09,140
We plan on returning 
to the spirit world for a while.

75
00:05:09,140 --> 00:05:10,020
What?

76
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:11,120
Don't worry.

77
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:14,830
I'll still bring medicine enough
 for our domain.

78
00:05:15,570 --> 00:05:17,790
How do you intend on dealing 
with the royal family?

79
00:05:17,790 --> 00:05:22,310
I informed His Highness that the crown
must pay for any further medicine we provide.

80
00:05:22,310 --> 00:05:26,000
I want him to reflect on his mistake, though,
so we won't supply any for a while yet.

81
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,010
Ellen...

82
00:05:32,650 --> 00:05:34,440
Thank you, Ellen.

83
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:40,010
Hey, what's goin' on?

84
00:05:40,010 --> 00:05:42,730
Is it true that the royal 
family took the medicine?

85
00:05:42,990 --> 00:05:44,690
Yes, it is.

86
00:05:43,970 --> 00:05:45,410
Please, I beg you!

87
00:05:45,410 --> 00:05:48,240
All because my daughter was 
kidnapped...

88
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,160
I'm sorry!

89
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:51,940
Please raise your head, Your Grace.

90
00:05:51,530 --> 00:05:53,930
Do something about this!

91
00:05:51,940 --> 00:05:54,500
What the heck is the royal family thinking?!

92
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:56,870
Please do something about this!

93
00:05:58,610 --> 00:06:00,010
Yeah, that's right.

94
00:06:00,010 --> 00:06:02,530
The royal family snatched up every last bit

95
00:06:02,530 --> 00:06:04,760
of medicine from the Vankreifts'
 treatment center.

96
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:05,630
You're kidding!

97
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:08,660
I heard it directly from the 
people working there.

98
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:09,870
There's no doubt about it.

99
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:12,030
Then the royal family is...

100
00:06:12,030 --> 00:06:14,220
Hoarding it all for themselves, I'm sure!

101
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:15,540
What the heck?

102
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:17,740
I hear the royal family 
is hoarding the medicine.

103
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:19,080
All when the disease is spreading!

104
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:21,040
What in the world is the royal family thinking?

105
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:22,890
What are we supposed to do?

106
00:06:22,890 --> 00:06:24,970
They're just trying to save themselves.

107
00:06:24,970 --> 00:06:26,620
What a cowardly thing to do!

108
00:06:26,950 --> 00:06:28,840
It's all the royal family's fault!

109
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,280
The royal family is to blame!

110
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:31,480
Yeah, the royal family!

111
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:31,480
Hand over the medicine!

112
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:31,990
The royals!

113
00:06:31,990 --> 00:06:34,620
We have no medicine here.

114
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:35,360
Lies! Hand it over!

115
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:36,330
It has to be somewhere!

116
00:06:36,330 --> 00:06:37,800
Hand over the medicine!

117
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,860
We know it's here!

118
00:06:47,470 --> 00:06:49,110
Don't be rough with them.

119
00:06:49,110 --> 00:06:49,680
Understood.

120
00:06:52,470 --> 00:06:53,320
Your Majesty!

121
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:57,930
Those who are ill are gathering 
at the castle seeking medicine.

122
00:06:58,790 --> 00:07:01,170
Open the treatment centers
 on the castle grounds.

123
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:03,220
Send in the court healers as well.

124
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:06,190
They're all demanding 
that we hand over the medicine...

125
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:12,820
We have no medicine to give them,
but treat them as best you can.

126
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:13,720
Sire.

127
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:20,580
But a drop in the ocean, is it not?

128
00:07:24,830 --> 00:07:25,900
Ellen, dear...

129
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:30,020
Mother.

130
00:07:30,020 --> 00:07:31,430
This must be so hard for you.

131
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:35,180
But you made the right decision, my dear Ellen.

132
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:37,820
Mr. Blackheart is to blame 
for taking it all too far.

133
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:40,980
You have no right to do this!

134
00:07:39,710 --> 00:07:40,980
This is horrible!

135
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:43,030
Hey! Say something!

136
00:07:43,870 --> 00:07:46,420
Stop messing with us!

137
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:52,400
I...

138
00:07:53,210 --> 00:07:57,520
In order to make clear the positions 
of the royal family and the spirits,

139
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:59,870
I have done all I could 
for the sake of our future.

140
00:08:01,110 --> 00:08:05,380
So why does my heart...

141
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:11,130
You are my pride and joy.

142
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:14,180
My kind, smart, darling daughter.

143
00:08:14,710 --> 00:08:16,200
Mother!

144
00:08:18,910 --> 00:08:22,840
I'm sorry for placing you in the middle
 between humans and spirits.

145
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:26,630
However, there are times when 
one must be ruthless.

146
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:28,480
You understand that, don't you?

147
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:33,560
I understand. I do understand. But...

148
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:36,070
Hand over the medicine you're hiding!

149
00:08:36,070 --> 00:08:38,920
You're gonna leave us to die?!

150
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:44,220
I knew it. We can't quell
 the riots without medicine.

151
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:47,540
Your Highness! Permission to report!

152
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:50,710
The messenger we sent to the 
Vankreift family has returned!

153
00:08:51,270 --> 00:08:52,050
And the medicine?

154
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:56,420
They said that Lord Rovel is away gathering
ingredients for the medicine

155
00:08:56,420 --> 00:08:58,140
and thus could not negotiate.

156
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:03,910
I see.

157
00:09:09,610 --> 00:09:10,520
What is going on?

158
00:09:11,580 --> 00:09:12,730
What is this ingredient?

159
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:14,180
Did you figure it out?

160
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:14,950
No.

161
00:09:28,190 --> 00:09:31,530
The princess doesn't smile much anymore.

162
00:09:40,170 --> 00:09:41,850
Oh, Van.

163
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:50,430
<i>I know. I'm worrying everyone.</i>

164
00:09:58,110 --> 00:09:59,080
She laughed!

165
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:00,750
The princess laughed!

166
00:10:00,750 --> 00:10:02,580
She laughed, she laughed!

167
00:10:02,580 --> 00:10:06,470
She laughed, yay!

168
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:14,060
Hey!

169
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:16,300
Oh yeah?!

170
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:19,130
Tickle, tickle, tickle, tickle, 
tickle, tickle, tickle, tickle!

171
00:10:23,650 --> 00:10:27,010
Oh, Van. Goodness!

172
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:30,780
You finally smiled, my princess.

173
00:10:31,450 --> 00:10:34,190
A smile really does suit 
you best, Ellen, dear.

174
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:37,030
Father, Mother...

175
00:10:45,450 --> 00:10:48,660
I'm sorry, Father! Mother!

176
00:10:49,830 --> 00:10:53,420
You know, Ori and I were just 
saying that maybe this is enough.

177
00:10:55,370 --> 00:10:59,240
This incident has dealt him a hard blow.

178
00:10:59,550 --> 00:11:01,850
Yet here you regret your decision.

179
00:11:05,390 --> 00:11:09,160
This had to be done 
in order to corner the king.

180
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:12,020
Still, it pains you to sow discontent 
among the people

181
00:11:12,020 --> 00:11:15,560
and to see them in anguish, 
doesn't it, Ellen?

182
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:16,750
Yes.

183
00:11:17,770 --> 00:11:19,850
You really are kind, Ellen.

184
00:11:21,090 --> 00:11:27,030
Up until now, I thought the only people 
important to me were you and Ori.

185
00:11:27,670 --> 00:11:30,620
I'd fallen into despair after 
witnessing man's true nature.

186
00:11:31,770 --> 00:11:35,000
But you know what, Ellen?
 I managed to remember something.

187
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:38,220
How I felt long ago.

188
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:40,250
That's all thanks to you, Ellen.

189
00:11:41,970 --> 00:11:48,560
Seeing how deeply you care for my mother, 
Sauvel, and the rest of the Vankreift family,

190
00:11:49,290 --> 00:11:56,450
I remembered why I risked my life to protect
 people during the Monster Tempest.

191
00:11:57,690 --> 00:12:04,280
You are daughter to us both, so it's only
 natural that you cherish both sides.

192
00:12:05,250 --> 00:12:07,740
Father, Mother...

193
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:10,610
Your Majesty!

194
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:13,920
Someone! Anyone! Summon the healer!

195
00:12:14,270 --> 00:12:16,040
Your Majesty! Please hang in there!

196
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:17,060
Your Majesty!

197
00:12:21,910 --> 00:12:23,030
Hurry!

198
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:27,650
The people are suffering!

199
00:12:27,650 --> 00:12:30,270
Even if it's just food supplies, 
deliver them with haste—

200
00:12:31,170 --> 00:12:32,220
Your Highness!

201
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:33,230
Are you all right?!

202
00:12:36,450 --> 00:12:38,990
Your Highness, please do not push yourself!

203
00:12:38,990 --> 00:12:40,430
Please go rest.

204
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:53,390
Where's the medicine?

205
00:12:53,390 --> 00:12:56,280
There isn't any left.

206
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,760
How can that be?

207
00:12:57,760 --> 00:13:00,860
I have a report saying
 it was all used up in experiments

208
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:04,090
trying to figure out how to reproduce it.

209
00:13:04,090 --> 00:13:06,180
My word...

210
00:13:07,730 --> 00:13:11,360
Have you wasted 
all of the medicine I gave you?

211
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:13,260
It certainly appears that way.

212
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:16,850
Lord Rovel the hero?

213
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:21,320
I should have sent someone
 who was familiar with the process.

214
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:24,070
This is why we told you 
you weren't capable of making it.

215
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:31,700
Goodness me. How rare to see 
His Majesty in bed.

216
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:33,930
Father, that's not appropriate.

217
00:13:33,930 --> 00:13:35,160
Could it be...

218
00:13:35,550 --> 00:13:39,580
Might this young lady here 
be the Healing Princess?

219
00:13:39,930 --> 00:13:42,050
P-Please!

220
00:13:42,730 --> 00:13:45,010
I beg of you, give us the medicine!

221
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:49,390
That's the first thing out of his mouth, huh?

222
00:13:49,390 --> 00:13:52,180
Well, I suppose with 
His Majesty in this state...

223
00:13:52,730 --> 00:13:53,950
But are you sure about this?

224
00:13:53,950 --> 00:13:57,060
We are technically trespassing, after all.

225
00:13:57,060 --> 00:13:58,140
Well...

226
00:13:58,400 --> 00:14:01,860
I suppose if you kick us out now,
 you'd never get the medicine you need.

227
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:05,330
Very well then.

228
00:14:08,010 --> 00:14:10,620
These two are separate medicines.

229
00:14:10,620 --> 00:14:14,410
Administer one pill of each three
 times a day, and give them together.

230
00:14:14,410 --> 00:14:16,120
Y-Yes, ma'am!

231
00:14:19,670 --> 00:14:22,090
Th-Thank you so much!

232
00:14:22,420 --> 00:14:26,050
L-Lord Rovel, you have my gratitude
 from the bottom of my heart!

233
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:28,510
If you're grateful, thank Ellen.

234
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:31,970
Don't play with it this time.

235
00:14:39,470 --> 00:14:41,610
This was the right thing to do, right?

236
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:44,740
Well, he's certainly suffering 
some consequences.

237
00:14:48,650 --> 00:14:50,060
Father...

238
00:14:50,060 --> 00:14:51,330
All right then!

239
00:14:51,330 --> 00:14:54,850
I'm going to go deliver medicine
 to Sauvel right now.

240
00:14:55,270 --> 00:14:59,380
I'll tell him to start accepting patients 
a little at a time from outside our land.

241
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:01,290
Yes. Please do.

242
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:04,100
You go take a break, Ellen.

243
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:10,590
Father, I'm sorry.

244
00:15:13,410 --> 00:15:15,560
I have an errand to run myself.

245
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:26,100
How are you feeling, Your Highness?

246
00:15:31,870 --> 00:15:32,780
Ellen!

247
00:15:35,170 --> 00:15:37,910
Am I... dreaming?

248
00:15:38,430 --> 00:15:41,070
Your Highness, don't you think this situation

249
00:15:41,070 --> 00:15:45,020
is similar to the Monster Tempest 
from two hundred years ago?

250
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:52,050
<i>She's right. Back then it was monsters,
and now we face a epidemic.</i>

251
00:15:52,770 --> 00:15:56,350
<i>We're drowning in fear, and again, 
trying to rely on the spirits' power. </i>

252
00:15:56,770 --> 00:16:02,270
Do you think things may have been different 
if the royal family and the spirits

253
00:16:02,580 --> 00:16:04,650
had spoken beforehand like this back then?

254
00:16:05,190 --> 00:16:08,150
At the very least, I don't 
think the royal family would have

255
00:16:08,150 --> 00:16:11,360
resorted to such cruel 
treatment of the spirits.

256
00:16:14,030 --> 00:16:17,070
We wanted you spirits so badly.

257
00:16:17,070 --> 00:16:21,290
The power of the spirits, 
the power that name brings...

258
00:16:22,370 --> 00:16:26,760
Every time we tried to take it by force, 
we ended up hurting you.

259
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:28,120
And even now—

260
00:16:38,990 --> 00:16:42,760
We will monitor the disease
so that it does not spread any further.

261
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:46,600
Just a moment ago, we delivered 
medicine to your court healer.

262
00:16:47,870 --> 00:16:50,190
You did? Thank you!

263
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:54,900
Once you recover, let us discuss 
our future dealings, Your Highness.

264
00:16:55,380 --> 00:16:57,290
You'd allow us to negotiate with you?

265
00:16:57,290 --> 00:17:00,950
That said, we will be driving 
a hard bargain. Is that understood?

266
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:05,170
Yes, of course.

267
00:17:09,030 --> 00:17:10,260
Hey, Ellen?

268
00:17:10,570 --> 00:17:11,990
What is it?

269
00:17:12,330 --> 00:17:16,800
If... If I'm able to gain your trust, 
even if it's just a little at a time...

270
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:21,260
Can we talk like this again?

271
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:28,080
It'd be a conversation 
held at this distance...

272
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:30,020
I don't mind! Even then!

273
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:42,670
That'll be all for today.

274
00:17:43,770 --> 00:17:46,430
I'll be back another time with my father.

275
00:17:47,330 --> 00:17:48,120
All right.

276
00:17:48,790 --> 00:17:50,930
Take care, Your Highness.

277
00:18:03,070 --> 00:18:04,020
Princess.

278
00:18:04,370 --> 00:18:06,070
Oh, Van!

279
00:18:06,070 --> 00:18:07,910
Did something happen?

280
00:18:07,910 --> 00:18:09,150
Huh? Like what?

281
00:18:09,770 --> 00:18:11,530
Your face is red.

282
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:12,610
What?!

283
00:18:12,950 --> 00:18:14,950
Did something good happen?

284
00:18:14,950 --> 00:18:17,550
N-No, nothing!

285
00:18:17,550 --> 00:18:19,110
Maybe it's because I'm sleepy.

286
00:18:19,110 --> 00:18:21,090
Oh, is that so?

287
00:18:24,330 --> 00:18:26,750
<i>Maybe it's because the 
unsettling feeling that's been</i>

288
00:18:26,750 --> 00:18:29,870
<i>building inside of me has 
completely cleared away...</i>

289
00:18:33,310 --> 00:18:37,290
I asked Sauvel to resume treatment 
within the Vankreift domain.

290
00:18:37,290 --> 00:18:41,890
Also, I had them spread the word 
that we're ready to accept patients.

291
00:18:41,890 --> 00:18:45,240
Very good. Then let us get to work.

292
00:18:48,650 --> 00:18:49,630
Princess.

293
00:18:49,950 --> 00:18:51,150
You called?

294
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:54,400
There's something I'd like 
to ask the both of you to do.

295
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:56,520
First, Leben, I would like you to restore

296
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:59,690
the physical strength of all the 
patients within the Vankreift territory

297
00:18:59,690 --> 00:19:02,430
and increase their natural healing ability.

298
00:19:02,430 --> 00:19:04,080
I'd be happy to.

299
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:08,350
Krelen, I'd like you to treat the 
seriously ill patients amongst them.

300
00:19:08,350 --> 00:19:09,540
Understood.

301
00:19:10,180 --> 00:19:13,290
Now, let us bring back everyone's smiles!

302
00:19:15,410 --> 00:19:16,630
Off we go!

303
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:26,170
<i>I asked the two of them to make sure the 
recovery from the illness appeared natural. </i>

304
00:19:26,170 --> 00:19:31,600
<i>But since it could lead to a riot,
 I had the spirits put up</i>

305
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:35,670
<i>a barrier to trigger their magic
 when a patient enters our domain.</i>

306
00:19:36,350 --> 00:19:39,280
<i>Furthermore, to heal the land
 neglected due to the disease,</i>

307
00:19:39,630 --> 00:19:45,500
<i>I first refined nitrogen, phosphorus,
 potassium, magnesium,</i>

308
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:48,230
<i>and calcium to serve as fertilizer. </i>

309
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:53,630
<i>I then had Borden the earth spirit 
spread it evenly over the fields.</i>

310
00:19:54,130 --> 00:19:56,810
<i>With action from the rain spirits,
 Niesel and Regen,</i>

311
00:19:56,810 --> 00:20:02,820
<i>the light spirit, Licht, 
and the plant spirits, Fran and Opst,</i>

312
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:07,270
<i>our crops grew abundant in no time.</i>

313
00:20:08,310 --> 00:20:12,100
<i>To help the struggling citizens, 
Uncle Sauvel issued a decree</i>

314
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:15,900
<i>allowing them to pay their taxes 
in crops for a time.</i>

315
00:20:16,370 --> 00:20:20,940
<i>The harvested produce
 was then distributed to the needy.</i>

316
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:23,710
<i>And as for the money the domain needed,</i>

317
00:20:23,710 --> 00:20:26,620
<i>we earned it by selling 
medicine to the royal family. </i>

318
00:20:26,940 --> 00:20:30,330
No, I'm afraid I cannot accept that price.

319
00:20:32,070 --> 00:20:36,460
Duke Sauvel, you truly are 
skilled at driving a bargain.

320
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:45,540
<i>After repeating this cycle for some time,
 the epidemic eventually subsided. </i>

321
00:20:47,330 --> 00:20:48,640
<i>And then...</i>

322
00:20:49,370 --> 00:20:50,960
Is that true?!

323
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:55,820
Yes, there has been a massive influx of 
people to the Vankreift domain.

324
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:00,490
<i>Thanks to their bountiful fields,</i>

325
00:21:00,490 --> 00:21:04,350
<i>our farmers were always shorthanded, 
which brought people flocking to the area.</i>

326
00:21:04,350 --> 00:21:09,710
<i>More people brought merchants,
 which brought life back to the town.</i>

327
00:21:09,710 --> 00:21:11,290
<i>Thanks to all this,</i>

328
00:21:11,290 --> 00:21:15,230
<i>the Vankreift domain has become known 
as the most livable place in the country.</i>

329
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:25,670
To think they managed to use the epidemic 
to develop their own territory...

330
00:21:25,670 --> 00:21:29,650
Do you finally understand, Your Majesty?

331
00:21:29,650 --> 00:21:30,310
Rovel.

332
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:33,150
I believe I told you before—

333
00:21:33,150 --> 00:21:35,270
You have no chance of winning against Ellen.

334
00:21:38,770 --> 00:21:39,790
So be it.

335
00:21:40,120 --> 00:21:43,190
From now on, the royal family 
will make no overture to Ellen.

336
00:21:44,060 --> 00:21:45,150
I swear by it.

337
00:21:45,970 --> 00:21:48,510
You seem to be feeling a lot better.

338
00:21:49,140 --> 00:21:51,410
Yes, all because of the medicine.

339
00:21:52,150 --> 00:21:52,920
I thank you.

340
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:55,530
Tch, what kind of a reply is that?

341
00:21:55,970 --> 00:21:57,220
This is no fun at all.

342
00:22:04,290 --> 00:22:06,060
Fluffy!

343
00:22:06,060 --> 00:22:08,370
You worked so hard, princess.

344
00:22:08,370 --> 00:22:10,280
Fluff away all you like!

345
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:14,460
Thank you, Van! Fluffy, fluffy, fluff, fluff!

346
00:22:12,450 --> 00:22:15,150
She really managed to do it all.

347
00:22:15,150 --> 00:22:18,100
My sweet Ellen is the best!

348
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:22,120
She loves all spirits and humans alike.

349
00:22:22,470 --> 00:22:25,150
She's proving through her very 
existence that we can

350
00:22:25,150 --> 00:22:27,110
mutually understand and support one another.

351
00:22:29,300 --> 00:22:31,070
My daughter is amazing.

352
00:22:31,340 --> 00:22:33,880
Yes, of course she is!

353
00:22:35,670 --> 00:22:37,620
Father! Mother!

354
00:22:39,570 --> 00:22:43,930
Let's go see everyone in the 
Vankreift family right now!

355
00:22:46,110 --> 00:22:49,570
